            "review_title": "Review at Hu tieu Nam Vang - Truong Phat - Truong Cong Dinh",
            "review_text": "Nhu_Phuong\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam\n292 contributions\n0\nA nice local restaurant\nAug 2016 • Friends\nDon't mistaken this place with the giant restaurant just right next to it. Make sure you get into the much smaller one with a noodle cartwheel in front. \nOrder the \"dry\" or \"hang\" noodles with broth on the side (Hủ tiếu mỳ khô) instead of the noodle soup. This is one of the most popular Southern dishes influenced by Khmer cuisine. But trust me, I've tried it in Phnom Penh, our version is a lot better. \nOften, the toppings include pork, liver, heart, prawn and quail eggs. The noodles are egg noodles and tapioca rice noodles.\nOne portion is only about 1.5 USD, so ... very cheap and great local food. \nHighly recommended if you're lost in the area.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten August 11, 2016",
